  "method": "The same production relay runs on one thread with anonymous Darwin socketpairs. Only the maximum number of events passed to a data kevent poll during the scored drain varies. The callback allows 128 events and the read maximum is 512 KiB. Sixteen established download streams are ready before each drain. Array index zero inserts a one-byte reply after queuing all bulk data, before the first poll. Indices 1\u201316 inject it immediately after the corresponding successful bulk write. Counters stop at the single final empty poll. The fixture checks payload, flow identity and order for every stream and marker, then checks half-close, reverse data and teardown. Two passes per width in reverse order agree exactly. The 1 MiB offer keeps streams ready for a second read. Results describe work order and kernel call counts; there is no time, TCP, VM or process-scheduling measurement.",
